---

## First Use / First Run

Run the following command to generate your local tool index:

```powershell
# Windows (PowerShell)
powershell -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File "references/scripts/refresh-tool-index.ps1"
```

```bash
# Linux / macOS / Kali
bash references/scripts/refresh-tool-index.sh
```

---

## Generated Format

Windows (PowerShell) generate 8-column table:
| Tool | Belongs to skill | Function | Available | Path | Version | Source | Script Reference |

Linux/macOS (Bash) generates a 7-column table:
| Tool | Skill | Purpose | Available | Path | Version | Install hint |

Both come with a 'Capability Status' subtable, which includes MCP registration status and service online checks.

